The authoritative, per-release list is the CycloneDX SBOM published alongside
each release artifact and generated for every commit — it names every component
and its resolved version, which a hand-maintained list in this file would
misstate within a week. To inspect the dependency set of a working tree
directly, read the package manifests and the lockfile (`pnpm-lock.yaml`).

Components worth naming here because they ship inside the distributed
appliance rather than merely building it:

  - @electric-sql/pglite (Apache-2.0) — the embedded Postgres the self-host
    appliance runs on when no Postgres server is configured.
  - croner (MIT) — the in-process scheduler the appliance uses instead of an
    external orchestrator.
  - drizzle-orm (Apache-2.0) — the query layer over the ledger schema.
  - nodemailer (MIT) — the SMTP client behind the notification channel; the
    only mail library in the workspace.
  - @trigger.dev/sdk (Apache-2.0) — the task runtime used by the managed
    edition only. It is not part of the self-host appliance.

